sequenceDiagram
    actor Faculty as Faculty/Sender
    participant SA as Sender Application
    participant RC as Recipient Application
    actor Recipient
    participant Channel as Untrusted Communication Channel
    participant Store as Trusted Sender Public Key Store
    Note over Faculty,Recipient: Independent RSA-3072 key pairs are generated
    Faculty->>SA: Generate sender key pair
    Recipient->>RC: Generate recipient key pair
    SA-->>RC: Exchange public keys through trusted channel
    RC->>Store: Store verified sender public key
    Faculty->>SA: Select examination paper
    SA->>SA: Generate random AES-256 key and 12-byte nonce
    SA->>SA: AES-256-GCM encrypt paper with canonical metadata AAD
    SA->>SA: Wrap key with recipient RSA public key (OAEP-SHA256)
    SA->>SA: Construct package; sign canonical contents (RSA-PSS-SHA256)
    SA->>Channel: Transfer .secpkg
    Channel->>RC: Deliver package
    RC->>RC: Parse and validate package
    RC->>Store: Load trusted sender public key
    RC->>RC: Verify sender signature
    alt Signature failure
        RC-->>Recipient: Reject; no plaintext released
    else Signature valid
        RC->>RC: Unwrap AES key with recipient private key
        alt Incorrect recipient key
            RC-->>Recipient: Reject; no plaintext released
        else Correct recipient key
            RC->>RC: Authenticate and decrypt with AES-GCM
            alt GCM authentication failure
                RC-->>Recipient: Reject; no plaintext released
            else Authentication succeeds
                RC-->>Recipient: Save recovered paper atomically
            end
        end
    end
